---
# ansible-lint configuration for petedio-iac (PET-397).
#
# There is no `.ansible-lint-ignore`. It existed briefly and is gone: every finding it
# froze is now either fixed or annotated at its own site with `# noqa: <rule>` and the
# reason above it. A rule suppressed next to the code it applies to can be argued with;
# a path in an ignore file cannot.
#
# Eleven of those sites were deliberate, and the reasons are worth knowing before you
# "fix" one: `apt-get -s` is a simulation whose stdout gets parsed, `systemctl start
# --wait` propagates a oneshot's exit code where the module would discard it, and three
# tasks must run in-line because a handler would fire after the verification that depends
# on them.
#
# Run it the way CI does, from this directory:
#   ansible-galaxy collection install -r requirements.yml
#   ansible-lint roles/ playbooks/

skip_list:
  # Every one of the 29 roles here uses a hyphen — apt-hygiene, cluster-qdevice,
  # vault-unseal. That is the house convention, and renaming them would touch every
  # playbook that includes them, so the rule is off rather than 29 noqa comments.
  # Fires when a role is linted directly (`ansible-lint roles/claude-code`), which is
  # what you do while writing one.
  - role-name
